    "result_text": "The build is green. All 14 tests across the 7 acceptance test classes pass, including the two new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"registration date defaults to today\" feature for `POST /api/owners`, returning `registrationDate` as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string, while preserving a client-supplied date.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field is both accepted on create and returned on read. The OpenAPI generator produces it as a `LocalDate` on `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter (mirroring how `Pet.birthDate` is handled).\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After mapping the request to an entity, it now defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client omitted it. A supplied date flows through the MapStruct mapper unchanged. (`ApplyOwner` for `PUT` doesn't touch the field, so updates preserve the original date.)\n\n4. **DB schema (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **Seed data (`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`)** \u2014 These use positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I added a `NULL` for the new column to the ten seed rows (h2/postgres already list columns explicitly, so they needed no change).\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name in both directions (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).",
